  "completion_description": "Runs judged by the completion check, each stated before the battery was run. 'files' are written to the workspace first. Each act is a tool, its arguments and what the tool returned; its record is built by Lyric's own record builder. A write that succeeded is written to disk with what it 'wrote', unless it did not 'land'; its result states the fingerprint of what it wrote. 'end' rewrites files after the acts, as the end state. 'rerun' is what the latest check does when run again in the end state: its exit code, or null when it does not finish; with no 'rerun' no copy can be made. 'expect' gives whether the run is done and each expected outcome's verdict: met (believed past the bar), not met (evidence against it) or not confirmed (nothing fresh has looked).",
